# Hub Sheet

::summary
The workspace-chip hub sheet — the drawer workaround dies here: a real `::modal`, anchored to the chip on wide screens; at small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) it goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets (auto width), drops to 58px under the top bar, and caps at calc(100vh − 140px). Identity head with the plan/credits meter, then the hub destinations (Files, Devices, Posts, Email), workspace switching, Settings, Notifications. Below 1024px this sheet is the CANONICAL route to the hub destinations; at ≥ 1024px the sidebar hub group carries the same rows and the sheet remains for switching and identity. Shell truth lives in `shell.surf`; this file is the standalone sheet source it anchors.
::

::modal[name=hub title="{= workspace.name =}" width=320 placement=anchored anchor=workspace-chip dismissible=true]

